    {
      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the complement of the 42-degree angle.\n2. Determine the supplement of the complement.\n\n**Step 1: Determine the complement of the 42-degree angle.**\n\nThe complement of an angle is the angle that, when added to the original angle, equals 90 degrees. Therefore, we calculate the complement of 42 degrees as follows:\n\n\\[ 90^\\circ - 42^\\circ = 48^\\circ \\]\n\nSo, the complement of a 42-degree angle is 48 degrees.\n\n**Step 2: Determine the supplement of the complement.**\n\nThe supplement of an angle is the angle that, when added to the original angle, equals 180 degrees. Therefore, we calculate the supplement of 48 degrees as follows:\n\n\\[ 180^\\circ - 48^\\circ = 132^\\circ \\]\n\nSo, the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle is 132 degrees.\n\nTherefore, the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle is \\(\\boxed{132}\\).",
